Aims:
1. Investigate changes in IOP and ocular structures induced by short-term exposure to head-down bed rest and hypercapnia;
2. Investigate changes in cerebral blood flow and indirectly estimate ICP;
3. Evaluate the relationships between the measured ocular and cerebral outcomes.

Aims:
The maturation task will
(1) integrate the findings of multiple SANS countermeasure studies that are completed on the ISS;
(2) determine which countermeasure best mitigates the SANS risk;
(3) develop the requirements for the countermeasure;
(4) develop a final protocol to be used on exploration class missions; and
(5) present the findings at boards to transition to appropriate operations stakeholders, as required

